tools/tampermonkey/museum-of-twitter-archiver.user.js   # Browser script: 📋 Archive button on x.com → clipboard JSON
```

## Key Behaviors Worth Knowing

- **One renderer**: `UserTweetDisplay.svelte` renders tweets everywhere (public and admin previews); the admin-only duplicate `TweetDisplay.svelte` was removed.
- **Slugs are permanent**: editing a tweet never changes its slug, since the slug is the public URL people share.
- **Deleting a tweet** (`deleteTweet()` in `tweetAdmin.ts`) removes its featured-tweet rows first (those foreign keys have no cascade), then the tweet, then every media file it references (main, quote, replies) via `/admin/media-cleanup`.
- **Uploads happen before saving** in `/admin/parse` and `/admin/create` so previews work; Clear (and re-pasting in `/admin/parse`) deletes uploads that never made it into a saved tweet. Closing the tab mid-draft still leaves them behind.
- **Featured tweet rotation** happens when the homepage renders on the server (`getTodaysFeaturedTweet()`): one query when today's tweet is already set, a rotation (30-day no-repeat) when it's from an earlier UTC day or missing.
- **Keeping public pages lean** (decided Oct 2026 — keep it this way):
  - Public pages (`/`, `/[slug]`) get their data from server `load` functions and `/api/tweets`, and must not import `$lib/supabase.js` (directly or through a component/util) — that client is ~53KB gzipped. `getMediaUrl()` builds storage URLs by hand for the same reason. Admin pages still use the client directly.
  - Queries select `TWEET_COLUMNS` (`id, slug, title, markdown_content, created_at`), not `*`.
  - Public responses send `PUBLIC_CACHE` (`s-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=86400`), so Vercel's CDN serves most visits without running the function or querying Supabase; edits appear within about a minute. Don't add cookies or per-visitor content to public responses or they stop being cacheable.
  - Heavy, rarely used code is loaded on demand (`modern-screenshot` is imported only when someone clicks "Copy as image").
  - Tailwind utilities are admin-only (`admin.css`); public components use scoped `<style>` blocks and the theme variables.
  - Result: ~44KB gzipped JS for the homepage, ~40KB for a tweet page, ~6KB of global CSS.
- **Link previews** (`[slug]/+page.svelte`): the first media of the main post, then replies, then the quoted tweet (`previewMedia()` in `media.ts`) is shown big at the top. Photos go through `/og/<slug>`, because chat apps shrink a roughly square image to a side thumbnail (Signal's rule: within 5% of square); there it's centred on a blurred copy of itself at 1200×630. A video goes in `og:video`. With no media the card uses the avatar (small thumbnail). Never put "on X" in the title.
- **Feed preferences** (sort order, theme) persist in `localStorage`, not per-user in the DB.
- **Two tweet-import paths**: manual markdown entry (`TweetCreator.svelte`, used by `/admin/create`) and clipboard-HTML import (`twitterClipboardParser.ts`, used by `/admin/parse`). Both end up writing the same `{title, slug, markdown_content}` shape to `tweets`.
- **Screenshot importer** (`/admin/screenshot`): the image is downscaled in the browser to stay under the API's own resize limit (1568px long edge / ~1.15MP) so the returned box coordinates match; boxes are kept in original-image pixels and the crops are cut from the original. Uses Claude Sonnet 5.5 at low effort (~1¢ per screenshot, ~1.5¢ for a thread). Handles threads/reply chains (stored as `[reply]` blocks); relative times like "1d" are kept as shown since there's no date to recover. Crops only upload on save (and are deleted again if the save fails).
- **Sharing**: the share button opens a small menu. "Copy link" copies `https://www.museumoftwitter.com/<slug>`; "Copy as image" renders the card (whole thread for threads) to a 2× PNG with `modern-screenshot` and writes it to the clipboard, falling back to downloading `<slug>.png` where image clipboard writes aren't allowed. The share button is kept in the image so the counts row looks the same as on the page. It relies on the `tweet-media` bucket sending `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` (it does); videos don't render into the image.
- **Engagement numbers**: the Tampermonkey script captures real counts; plain copy/paste doesn't carry them, so that path falls back to plausible synthetic numbers. The screenshot importer has Low/Medium/High buttons (per post, for threads) that fill in made-up counts via `randomEngagement()`; clicking again re-rolls.
- **Admin writes use the plain anon-key client** (`$lib/supabase.js`), not a session-bound server client — write authorization is enforced by Supabase RLS policies, not by SvelteKit. The page-level session gate in `admin/+layout.server.js` only protects rendering the admin UI.

## Environment variables

`PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (needed at build time), `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (server-only, read at request time by `/admin/screenshot-extract`). Set all three in Vercel and in the local `.env`.

## Storage policies

`tweet-media` needs SELECT (public), INSERT (public, used by the anon client), and DELETE for `authenticated` only — deletes go through `/admin/media-cleanup`, which acts as the logged-in admin.

## Known Cleanup Candidates (not yet done — require a live-DB change, so flagged rather than applied)
- **RLS on `tweets`/`current_featured_tweet`/`featured_tweet_history` is fully open** to the `public` role (see Database Schema above) — the biggest one, since it means the admin login doesn't actually gate writes at the data layer.
- `tweets.parsed_json` and `tweets.tweet_date` columns (plus the GIN index on `parsed_json`) are live in the DB but unused by any code path.
- `tweets` has a redundant index: `idx_tweets_slug` duplicates the index the `UNIQUE (slug)` constraint already creates (`tweets_slug_key`).
- `current_featured_tweet.tweet_id` / `featured_tweet_history.tweet_id` foreign keys could be `ON DELETE CASCADE`; `deleteTweet()` works around it by deleting those rows first.

Already fixed: the old unused `types/tweet.ts` and `TweetParser.svelte` (plus the `@tiptap/*` deps) were deleted; `.sql` reflects the verified live schema; `TweetDisplay.svelte` was folded into `UserTweetDisplay.svelte`; the global `!important` theme overrides in `app.css` were removed.

## Roadmap / open items
Ordered roughly by importance. Move items to "Already fixed" (or delete them) when done.

1. **Lock down writes** — the RLS item above: policies that require `authenticated` for writes, plus admin mutations through a session-bound client. Needs a coordinated live-DB change (shared Supabase project — get explicit sign-off first).
2. **Orphaned uploads** — closing the tab mid-draft in `/admin/parse` or `/admin/create` leaves uploaded files in `tweet-media`. A periodic admin "find unreferenced files" sweep (list the bucket, diff against `referencedMediaFiles()` over all tweets) would catch them.
3. **Link previews for threads** — the description is only the first post's text; media now comes from the whole thread (see Link previews above).
4. **Copy as image with video** — videos come out blank; could swap in a poster frame before capturing.
5. **Featured-tweet rotation** runs during a server render; with the CDN cache that's at most once a minute, but two cold renders right after midnight UTC could still both rotate. A Vercel cron job would make it exactly once a day.
6. **DB cleanup** — drop the unused `parsed_json`/`tweet_date` columns and the redundant slug index (see above).
